        "original_id": "654db33c-aa6a-56a2-b233-86a5b0b8480e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ernie Hine\n- Organizations: Manchester United F.C.\n- Places: Old Trafford, Greater Manchester, England\n- Topics: English football\n\nFacts:\n- Ernie Hine was born on 9 April 1901 and died on 15 April 1974.\n- Manchester United F.C. was founded as Newton Heath LYR Football Club in 1878.\n- Manchester United F.C. changed its name to Manchester United in 1902.\n- Manchester United F.C. moved to Old Trafford in 1910.\n- Ernie Hine was a professional footballer who played for Barnsley, Leicester City, Huddersfield Town, and Manchester United.\n- Manchester United F.C. is nicknamed \"the Red Devils.\"\n- Manchester United F.C. is a professional football club based in Old Trafford, Greater Manchester, England.\n- Manchester United F.C. competes in the Premier League, the top flight of English football.",
